    "body": "Hi @Nazar65 the condition `empty($value['tmp_name']) && !is_uploaded_file($value['tmp_name'])` will evaluate to:\r\n - `false` is  `$value['tmp_name']` is set\r\n - `true`if `$value['tmp_name']` is empty\r\n\r\nThe second part of the condition will be checked only if `$value['tmp_name']` is empty, that does not make sense in this case.\r\n\r\nThat's why I suggest changing this condition to fail validation in both cases if `tmp_name` is empty or file is not uploaded\r\n```suggestion\r\n        if (empty($value['tmp_name']) || !is_uploaded_file($value['tmp_name'])) {\r\n```",
